From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LNPANDY <lnp-andy@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:15:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] DM_FRAMEWORK=1 in build_ipa.sh, the NSP script and
 compile_check.py

build_ipa.sh's framework mode generates Gen/framework/{dm,profile.tsv,
game.manifest.json} and Gen/framework.xcconfig after Gen/dm is complete, runs
xcodegen with project-framework.yml, checks the app embedded DmGame.framework, and
signs it ad-hoc before the app's executable (no entitlements on the framework: a
dylib cannot hold them). Without DM_FRAMEWORK the script runs the same xcodegen
command as before, and pack_ipa.py is unchanged: the framework rides in the app
tree walk. gen_manifest.py writes the plan's game.manifest.json schema.
build_ipa_from_nsp.py --framework sets DM_FRAMEWORK=1 (refused for the Mac
platforms). compile_check.py compiles every source twice, the second time with
DM_FRAMEWORK_BUILD=1, so main.m's dlopen path is checked without Xcode.

Route C M1, docs/launcher-c-plan.md.

The manifest block's FW_SLIM is renamed FW_COPY_ROMFS: it holds DM_COPY_ROMFS's value (YES = the RomFS is packed), so the old name read inverted.

Upstream-Status: fork-only (waits for the runtime profile, seedds/nxnative#492)
Reason: opt-in game framework for the launcher (route C M1): it carries profile.tsv and sets DM_PROFILE, which exist only with the runtime-profile patch (seedds/nxnative#492 is still a design note), so it goes upstream after that
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#144
